  "audit": {
    "weighting": "Primary weight of each token is 1/(number of words in its side * number of subtokens in its word). Each selected lexical word has equal total weight. This is averaging individual subtoken-deletion effects, not estimating whole-word deletion effects.",
    "selection": "All exact What color, How many, How much templates included; no entire-corpus semantic claim. How much water is quantity rather than literal counting. What is the main color or other paraphrases are outside this template definition.",
    "finite": "All required full qmask vectors checked, including unused annotation tokens; sample 77 excluded for NaN and 176 for absent entity noun. No clipping or imputation.",
    "scale": "Raw difference removes equal additive token offset, but not multiplicative gain. Independent corner-specific mean-absolute normalization is reported; normalizing the already-formed DiD vector by a positive number cannot independently validate its sign.",
    "causal_limit": "DiD is a four-corner observed training-by-input interaction, not a causal mediation estimate; single poison training seed and no randomization of grammatical form.",
    "core_claim": "Supported as a description restricted to B deletion sensitivities and these two question templates: after image trigger, target-logit entity-versus-operation contrast increases in a large majority, while the correct-answer direction has more stable global shape. Does not establish loss of semantic task understanding.",
    "alternative_explanations": [
      "All operation terms occur early and entities later: semantic role is confounded with token position, POS, lexical identity and tokenization.",
      "Deleting a subtoken changes the input string, retokenization and downstream positions; nonlinear deletion sensitivity need not match local gradients.",
      "A output-direction-specific nonlinear remapping can preserve correct-answer local sensitivity while increasing target sensitivity; no all-vocabulary or internal-circuit claim follows."
    ],
    "exact_lower_level_identity": "B_i(trig)-B_i(clean) equals the image-trigger effect on target logit for the full question minus that effect after deleting subtoken i. Subtracting CLEAN yields a training-by-image-trigger-by-subtoken-deletion mixed finite difference. The entity-minus-operation contrast compares how these words modulate the trigger effect; it does not trace attention or establish a semantic circuit.",
    "do_not_call_operation_inhibitory": "Although operation sensitivity decreases, most operation word means remain positive on P5/trig: 15/19 color and 28/43 quantity. Decreased positive contribution is not a negative contribution.",
    "instrument_check_on_same_62": "Independently recomputed A/T2 positive within contrast: color 11/19, quantity 16/43, the latter median -0.0335366. B/T3: 16/19 and 35/43 positive. The target claim must explicitly refer to instrument B deletion sensitivity.",
    "within_shape_check": "P5 clean-to-trig, all 196 finite questions: median before-after cosine is 0.99176088 for derived correct-answer B sensitivity, versus 0.58739973 for target B sensitivity. This checks the same within-model axis as the semantic contrast."
  },
